# fs-9p: lines to add fs-9p to a QNX image (installed as
# share/fs-9p/fs-9p.build). Replace /opt/fs-9p with your installation
# prefix, hostshare with the mount tag given to QEMU, and /mnt/host with
# the mount point you want. Details: the User Guide, "Adding fs-9p to a
# QNX system".
#
# ---- mkqnximage images -------------------------------------------------------
# local/snippets/system_files.custom (the binary, in /system/bin):
#
#   [perms=0755] bin/fs-9p=/opt/fs-9p/sbin/fs-9p
#
# local/snippets/post_start.custom (mount at the end of startup):
#
#   fs-9p hostshare /mnt/host
#
# then: mkqnximage --build --noprompt
#
# ---- your own IFS buildfile ----------------------------------------------------
# In the startup script, before anything that uses the share:
#
#   fs-9p hostshare /mnt/host
#   waitfor /mnt/host 10
#
# In the file list (the binary, in /proc/boot):

[perms=0755] fs-9p=/opt/fs-9p/sbin/fs-9p
